INSERT INTO `remote_server_services` (`id`, `api_provider_id`, `remote_id`, `name`, `group_name`, `price`, `time`, `info`, `min_qty`, `max_qty`, `credit_groups`, `additional_fields`, `additional_data`, `params`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1182, 2, '207', 'Octoplus FRP 1 Year Digital License', 'Gsm Server Products', 55.0000, NULL, '<p><strong>Octoplus FRP 1 Year Digital License</strong>&nbsp;enables FRP reset operations for&nbsp;<strong>Samsung, Huawei, Xiaomi, LG, Alcatel, Motorola</strong>&nbsp;cell phones.</p>\r\n<p>This license will be bound to your PC. No dongle or box is required. After the end of 1 year period you will have to buy this license again.</p>\r\n<div class=\"notification\">\r\n<h2 data-id=\"0-pc-changing-policy\">PC Changing Policy</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>You can change a PC once per 48 hours (not more than 25 times during 1 year).</li>\r\n<li>The same license can be used on 2 PCs without switching limits.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Note!</strong>&nbsp;Huawei phones released after March 2018 with new security (except models supported via test point) are&nbsp;<strong>NOT SUPPORTED</strong>.<br />Please follow future updates for more information.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"activate\" data-id=\"11-how-to-activate\">How to Activate:</h2>\r\n<p>To start using your digital license, please follow these steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Download the latest version of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://octoplusbox.com/en/download/software/\">Octoplus FRP Tool Installer</a></li>\r\n<li>Launch the software</li>\r\n<li>Use the received string to activate your digital license</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div class=\"full-img\"><img src=\"https://f00.psgsm.net/product/894333/screenshot-60.jpg\" alt=\"Software\" /></div>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"1-samsung-reset-frp-operations\">Samsung Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"2--reset-frp-uart-ufs-chips-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\">1. &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</h3>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation, do the following steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Put the phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold \"Volume-\" + \"Home\" + \"Power ON\" buttons) and connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Press &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; button.</li>\r\n<li>After Software request disconnect USB cable and connect Samsung Micro UART cable.</li>\r\n<li>Press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; keys for 15-20 seconds, Software will automatically close wizard window and will perform the reset FRP lock.</li>\r\n<li>Done.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"3--reset-frp-adb-combination-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\">2. &ldquo;Reset FRP ADB (Combination)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</h3>\r\n<p>To Reset FRP lock using combination firmware, you can try to do the following:</p>\r\n<p>I.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Write \"boot.img\" partition from appropriate Combination firmware.</li>\r\n<li>Perform \"Reset FRP ADB (Combination)\" operation in the software.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>II.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Write full Combination firmware.</li>\r\n<li>Go to \"Developer Options\" in the phone&rsquo;s Settings.</li>\r\n<li>Check \"Enable OEM ...\" option.</li>\r\n<li>Perform Factory Data Reset.</li>\r\n<li>Reflash the phone with full stock (original) firmware.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: \"boot.img\" from combination firmware can be not compatible with current phone\'s firmware. In that case phone will freeze on logo, or will be rebooting after writing of such boot. To restore the phone to its initial condition you need to reflash it with different full stock (original) firmware (or try to write only boot of such firmware).</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also note</strong>: You can write \"boot.img\" combination firmware or downgrade phone\'s firmware version only at your own risk!</p>\r\n<p>P.S. If you cannot find combination firmware for your model in &ldquo;SAMSUNG/COMBINATION\" folder in Support Area, this means we don&rsquo;t have these files at the moment. As soon as we get new combination firmwares, we will upload them into the Support Area.</p>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"4--reset-frp-download-mode-operation-be-careful-performing-this-operation-will-delete-all-user-data-contacts-pictures-and-other-from-the-device\">3. &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation will delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) from the device!</h3>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<p>1. Click \"Reset FRP (Download Mode)\" button.<br />2. Put phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Home&rdquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; buttons).<br />3. Connect the phone to PC via Micro USB cable.<br />4. Follow Software instructions (prompts).</p>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"5-huawei-reset-frp-operations\">Huawei Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation may reset/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.</li>\r\n<li>Put the phone in FastBoot Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; button, insert USB cable and wait until the phone goes in FastBoot Mode).</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"6-lg-reset-frp-operations\">LG Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be carefully, performing this operation may reset/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<p>1. Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<br />2. Put the phone in Download Mode (power the phone OFF, press and hold \"Vol+\" button and connect USB cable).<br />3. Install necessary driver.<br />4. Click \"Reset FRP\" button.<br />5. Follow software instructions (prompts).</p>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"7--alcatel-reset-frp-operations\">Alcatel Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Power the phone OFF and connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button.</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"8-motorola-reset-frp-operations\">Motorola Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Put the phone in Factory Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold \"Vol-\" + \"Power\" buttons; select &ldquo;Factory Mode&rdquo; in phone&rsquo;s menu and confirm selection; wait until the phone powers ON).</li>\r\n<li>Connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button.</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>Note: &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation may not work for some devices with latest Security patch level.</p>\r\n<p>* Developer provides support only for those phones which are on the list of supported. Not all servicing features can be applied to some supported models, due to difference of hardware / software versions.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>#shandy</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"widget_product_octopus-models\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[]', '{\"SERVICEID\":207,\"SERVICENAME\":\"Octoplus FRP 1 Year Digital License\",\"CREDIT\":\"55.0000\",\"INFO\":\"<p><strong>Octoplus FRP 1 Year Digital License<\\/strong>&nbsp;enables FRP reset operations for&nbsp;<strong>Samsung, Huawei, Xiaomi, LG, Alcatel, Motorola<\\/strong>&nbsp;cell phones.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>This license will be bound to your PC. No dongle or box is required. After the end of 1 year period you will have to buy this license again.<\\/p>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"notification\\\">\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"0-pc-changing-policy\\\">PC Changing Policy<\\/h2>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li>You can change a PC once per 48 hours (not more than 25 times during 1 year).<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>The same license can be used on 2 PCs without switching limits.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p><strong>Note!<\\/strong>&nbsp;Huawei phones released after March 2018 with new security (except models supported via test point) are&nbsp;<strong>NOT SUPPORTED<\\/strong>.<br \\/>Please follow future updates for more information.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 id=\\\"activate\\\" data-id=\\\"11-how-to-activate\\\">How to Activate:<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>To start using your digital license, please follow these steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Download the latest version of&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/octoplusbox.com\\/en\\/download\\/software\\/\\\">Octoplus FRP Tool Installer<\\/a><\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Launch the software<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Use the received string to activate your digital license<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"full-img\\\"><img src=\\\"https:\\/\\/f00.psgsm.net\\/product\\/894333\\/screenshot-60.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"Software\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"1-samsung-reset-frp-operations\\\">Samsung Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-id=\\\"2--reset-frp-uart-ufs-chips-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\\\">1. &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation, do the following steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Put the phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold \\\"Volume-\\\" + \\\"Home\\\" + \\\"Power ON\\\" buttons) and connect USB cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Press &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; button.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>After Software request disconnect USB cable and connect Samsung Micro UART cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; keys for 15-20 seconds, Software will automatically close wizard window and will perform the reset FRP lock.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Done.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h3 data-id=\\\"3--reset-frp-adb-combination-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\\\">2. &ldquo;Reset FRP ADB (Combination)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p>To Reset FRP lock using combination firmware, you can try to do the following:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>I.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Write \\\"boot.img\\\" partition from appropriate Combination firmware.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Perform \\\"Reset FRP ADB (Combination)\\\" operation in the software.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p>II.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Write full Combination firmware.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Go to \\\"Developer Options\\\" in the phone&rsquo;s Settings.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Check \\\"Enable OEM ...\\\" option.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Perform Factory Data Reset.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Reflash the phone with full stock (original) firmware.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p><strong>Note<\\/strong>: \\\"boot.img\\\" from combination firmware can be not compatible with current phone\'s firmware. In that case phone will freeze on logo, or will be rebooting after writing of such boot. To restore the phone to its initial condition you need to reflash it with different full stock (original) firmware (or try to write only boot of such firmware).<\\/p>\\r\\n<p><strong>Also note<\\/strong>: You can write \\\"boot.img\\\" combination firmware or downgrade phone\'s firmware version only at your own risk!<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>P.S. If you cannot find combination firmware for your model in &ldquo;SAMSUNG\\/COMBINATION\\\" folder in Support Area, this means we don&rsquo;t have these files at the moment. As soon as we get new combination firmwares, we will upload them into the Support Area.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-id=\\\"4--reset-frp-download-mode-operation-be-careful-performing-this-operation-will-delete-all-user-data-contacts-pictures-and-other-from-the-device\\\">3. &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation will delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) from the device!<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>1. Click \\\"Reset FRP (Download Mode)\\\" button.<br \\/>2. Put phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Home&rdquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; buttons).<br \\/>3. Connect the phone to PC via Micro USB cable.<br \\/>4. Follow Software instructions (prompts).<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"5-huawei-reset-frp-operations\\\">Huawei Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation may reset\\/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Put the phone in FastBoot Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; button, insert USB cable and wait until the phone goes in FastBoot Mode).<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Install necessary driver.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"6-lg-reset-frp-operations\\\">LG Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be carefully, performing this operation may reset\\/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>1. Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<br \\/>2. Put the phone in Download Mode (power the phone OFF, press and hold \\\"Vol+\\\" button and connect USB cable).<br \\/>3. Install necessary driver.<br \\/>4. Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button.<br \\/>5. Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"7--alcatel-reset-frp-operations\\\">Alcatel Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Install necessary driver.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Power the phone OFF and connect USB cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"8-motorola-reset-frp-operations\\\">Motorola Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Put the phone in Factory Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold \\\"Vol-\\\" + \\\"Power\\\" buttons; select &ldquo;Factory Mode&rdquo; in phone&rsquo;s menu and confirm selection; wait until the phone powers ON).<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Connect USB cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Install necessary driver.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p>Note: &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation may not work for some devices with latest Security patch level.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>* Developer provides support only for those phones which are on the list of supported. Not all servicing features can be applied to some supported models, due to difference of hardware \\/ software versions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>#shandy<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"widget_product_octopus-models\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\",\"ADDITIONAL_NVP\":\"a:2:{s:13:\\\"hide_quantity\\\";i:0;s:13:\\\"quantity_rule\\\";a:4:{s:9:\\\"min_value\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:9:\\\"max_value\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:11:\\\"multiple_of\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:9:\\\"specified\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";}}\",\"TIME\":\"\",\"sync_key_data\":\"\",\"service_type_price_data\":\"\",\"qry_range_credit_info\":[{\"from_range\":1,\"to_range\":99,\"credit\":\"55.0000\"}],\"REQUIRED\":\"\"}', '{\"CUSTOM\":null}', '2026-02-25 03:00:52', '2026-02-25 03:00:52'),
(1183, 2, '477', 'Octoplus FRP 3 Month Digital License', 'Gsm Server Products', 30.0000, NULL, '<p><strong>Octoplus FRP 3 Month Digital License</strong>&nbsp;enables FRP (Google Factory Reset Protection) reset operations for&nbsp;<strong>Samsung, Huawei, Xiaomi, LG, Alcatel, Motorola</strong>&nbsp;cell phones.</p>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"0-general-information\">General Information</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>This license will be bound to your PC. No dongle or box is required.</li>\r\n<li>You can change a PC once per 48 hours (not more than 6 times during 3 months).</li>\r\n<li>The same license can be used on 2 PCs without switching limits.</li>\r\n<li>After the end of 3 month period you will have to buy this license again.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Note!</strong>&nbsp;Huawei phones released after March 2018 with new security (except models supported via test point) are&nbsp;<strong>NOT SUPPORTED</strong>.<br />Please follow future updates for more information</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"activate\" data-id=\"11-how-to-activate\">How to Activate:</h2>\r\n<p>To start using your digital license, please follow these steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Download the latest version of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://octoplusbox.com/en/download/software/\">Octoplus FRP Tool Installer</a></li>\r\n<li>Launch the software</li>\r\n<li>Use the received string to activate your digital license</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div class=\"full-img\"><img src=\"https://f00.psgsm.net/product/894333/screenshot-60.jpg\" alt=\"Software\" /></div>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"1-samsung-reset-frp-operations\">Samsung Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"2--reset-frp-uart-ufs-chips-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\">1. &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</h3>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation, do the following steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Put the phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold \"Volume-\" + \"Home\" + \"Power ON\" buttons) and connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Press &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; button.</li>\r\n<li>After Software request disconnect USB cable and connect Samsung Micro UART cable.</li>\r\n<li>Press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; keys for 15-20 seconds, Software will automatically close wizard window and will perform the reset FRP lock.</li>\r\n<li>Done.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"3--reset-frp-adb-combination-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\">2. &ldquo;Reset FRP ADB (Combination)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</h3>\r\n<p>To Reset FRP lock using combination firmware, you can try to do the following:</p>\r\n<p>I.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Write \"boot.img\" partition from appropriate Combination firmware.</li>\r\n<li>Perform \"Reset FRP ADB (Combination)\" operation in the software.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>II.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Write full Combination firmware.</li>\r\n<li>Go to \"Developer Options\" in the phone&rsquo;s Settings.</li>\r\n<li>Check \"Enable OEM ...\" option.</li>\r\n<li>Perform Factory Data Reset.</li>\r\n<li>Reflash the phone with full stock (original) firmware.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: \"boot.img\" from combination firmware can be not compatible with current phone\'s firmware. In that case phone will freeze on logo, or will be rebooting after writing of such boot. To restore the phone to its initial condition you need to reflash it with different full stock (original) firmware (or try to write only boot of such firmware).</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also note</strong>: You can write \"boot.img\" combination firmware or downgrade phone\'s firmware version only at your own risk!</p>\r\n<p>P.S. If you cannot find combination firmware for your model in &ldquo;SAMSUNG/COMBINATION\" folder in Support Area, this means we don&rsquo;t have these files at the moment. As soon as we get new combination firmwares, we will upload them into the Support Area.</p>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"4--reset-frp-download-mode-operation-be-careful-performing-this-operation-will-delete-all-user-data-contacts-pictures-and-other-from-the-device\">3. &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation will delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) from the device!</h3>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<p>1. Click \"Reset FRP (Download Mode)\" button.<br />2. Put phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Home&rdquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; buttons).<br />3. Connect the phone to PC via Micro USB cable.<br />4. Follow Software instructions (prompts).</p>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"5-huawei-reset-frp-operations\">Huawei Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation may reset/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.</li>\r\n<li>Put the phone in FastBoot Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; button, insert USB cable and wait until the phone goes in FastBoot Mode).</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"6-lg-reset-frp-operations\">LG Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be carefully, performing this operation may reset/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<p>1. Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<br />2. Put the phone in Download Mode (power the phone OFF, press and hold \"Vol+\" button and connect USB cable).<br />3. Install necessary driver.<br />4. Click \"Reset FRP\" button.<br />5. Follow software instructions (prompts).</p>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"7--alcatel-reset-frp-operations\">Alcatel Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Power the phone OFF and connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button.</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"8-motorola-reset-frp-operations\">Motorola Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Put the phone in Factory Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold \"Vol-\" + \"Power\" buttons; select &ldquo;Factory Mode&rdquo; in phone&rsquo;s menu and confirm selection; wait until the phone powers ON).</li>\r\n<li>Connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button.</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>Note: &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation may not work for some devices with latest Security patch level.</p>\r\n<p>* Developer provides support only for those phones which are on the list of supported. Not all servicing features can be applied to some supported models, due to difference of hardware / software versions.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>#shandy</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"widget_product_octopus-models\">&nbsp;</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[]', '{\"SERVICEID\":477,\"SERVICENAME\":\"Octoplus FRP 3 Month Digital License\",\"CREDIT\":\"30.0000\",\"INFO\":\"<p><strong>Octoplus FRP 3 Month Digital License<\\/strong>&nbsp;enables FRP (Google Factory Reset Protection) reset operations for&nbsp;<strong>Samsung, Huawei, Xiaomi, LG, Alcatel, Motorola<\\/strong>&nbsp;cell phones.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"0-general-information\\\">General Information<\\/h2>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li>This license will be bound to your PC. No dongle or box is required.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>You can change a PC once per 48 hours (not more than 6 times during 3 months).<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>The same license can be used on 2 PCs without switching limits.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>After the end of 3 month period you will have to buy this license again.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p><strong>Note!<\\/strong>&nbsp;Huawei phones released after March 2018 with new security (except models supported via test point) are&nbsp;<strong>NOT SUPPORTED<\\/strong>.<br \\/>Please follow future updates for more information<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 id=\\\"activate\\\" data-id=\\\"11-how-to-activate\\\">How to Activate:<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>To start using your digital license, please follow these steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Download the latest version of&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/octoplusbox.com\\/en\\/download\\/software\\/\\\">Octoplus FRP Tool Installer<\\/a><\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Launch the software<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Use the received string to activate your digital license<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"full-img\\\"><img src=\\\"https:\\/\\/f00.psgsm.net\\/product\\/894333\\/screenshot-60.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"Software\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"1-samsung-reset-frp-operations\\\">Samsung Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-id=\\\"2--reset-frp-uart-ufs-chips-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\\\">1. &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation, do the following steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Put the phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold \\\"Volume-\\\" + \\\"Home\\\" + \\\"Power ON\\\" buttons) and connect USB cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Press &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; button.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>After Software request disconnect USB cable and connect Samsung Micro UART cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; keys for 15-20 seconds, Software will automatically close wizard window and will perform the reset FRP lock.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Done.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h3 data-id=\\\"3--reset-frp-adb-combination-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\\\">2. &ldquo;Reset FRP ADB (Combination)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p>To Reset FRP lock using combination firmware, you can try to do the following:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>I.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Write \\\"boot.img\\\" partition from appropriate Combination firmware.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Perform \\\"Reset FRP ADB (Combination)\\\" operation in the software.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p>II.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Write full Combination firmware.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Go to \\\"Developer Options\\\" in the phone&rsquo;s Settings.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Check \\\"Enable OEM ...\\\" option.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Perform Factory Data Reset.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Reflash the phone with full stock (original) firmware.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p><strong>Note<\\/strong>: \\\"boot.img\\\" from combination firmware can be not compatible with current phone\'s firmware. In that case phone will freeze on logo, or will be rebooting after writing of such boot. To restore the phone to its initial condition you need to reflash it with different full stock (original) firmware (or try to write only boot of such firmware).<\\/p>\\r\\n<p><strong>Also note<\\/strong>: You can write \\\"boot.img\\\" combination firmware or downgrade phone\'s firmware version only at your own risk!<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>P.S. If you cannot find combination firmware for your model in &ldquo;SAMSUNG\\/COMBINATION\\\" folder in Support Area, this means we don&rsquo;t have these files at the moment. As soon as we get new combination firmwares, we will upload them into the Support Area.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-id=\\\"4--reset-frp-download-mode-operation-be-careful-performing-this-operation-will-delete-all-user-data-contacts-pictures-and-other-from-the-device\\\">3. &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation will delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) from the device!<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>1. Click \\\"Reset FRP (Download Mode)\\\" button.<br \\/>2. Put phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Home&rdquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; buttons).<br \\/>3. Connect the phone to PC via Micro USB cable.<br \\/>4. Follow Software instructions (prompts).<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"5-huawei-reset-frp-operations\\\">Huawei Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation may reset\\/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Put the phone in FastBoot Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; button, insert USB cable and wait until the phone goes in FastBoot Mode).<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Install necessary driver.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"6-lg-reset-frp-operations\\\">LG Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be carefully, performing this operation may reset\\/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>1. Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<br \\/>2. Put the phone in Download Mode (power the phone OFF, press and hold \\\"Vol+\\\" button and connect USB cable).<br \\/>3. Install necessary driver.<br \\/>4. Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button.<br \\/>5. Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"7--alcatel-reset-frp-operations\\\">Alcatel Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Install necessary driver.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Power the phone OFF and connect USB cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"8-motorola-reset-frp-operations\\\">Motorola Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Put the phone in Factory Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold \\\"Vol-\\\" + \\\"Power\\\" buttons; select &ldquo;Factory Mode&rdquo; in phone&rsquo;s menu and confirm selection; wait until the phone powers ON).<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Connect USB cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Install necessary driver.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p>Note: &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation may not work for some devices with latest Security patch level.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>* Developer provides support only for those phones which are on the list of supported. Not all servicing features can be applied to some supported models, due to difference of hardware \\/ software versions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>#shandy<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"widget_product_octopus-models\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div>\",\"ADDITIONAL_NVP\":\"a:2:{s:13:\\\"hide_quantity\\\";i:0;s:13:\\\"quantity_rule\\\";a:4:{s:9:\\\"min_value\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:9:\\\"max_value\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:11:\\\"multiple_of\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:9:\\\"specified\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";}}\",\"TIME\":\"\",\"sync_key_data\":\"\",\"service_type_price_data\":\"\",\"qry_range_credit_info\":[{\"from_range\":1,\"to_range\":99,\"credit\":\"30.0000\"}],\"REQUIRED\":\"\"}', '{\"CUSTOM\":null}', '2026-02-25 03:00:52', '2026-02-25 03:00:52');
INSERT INTO `remote_server_services` (`id`, `api_provider_id`, `remote_id`, `name`, `group_name`, `price`, `time`, `info`, `min_qty`, `max_qty`, `credit_groups`, `additional_fields`, `additional_data`, `params`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1184, 2, '202', 'Octoplus FRP 6 Month Digital License', 'Gsm Server Products', 47.0000, NULL, '<p><strong>Octoplus FRP 6 Month Digital License</strong>&nbsp;enables FRP reset operations for&nbsp;<strong>Samsung, Huawei, Xiaomi, LG, Alcatel, Motorola</strong>&nbsp;cell phones.</p>\r\n<div class=\"yt-video -inside-dom\" data-video-id=\"czL9Sp7hesA\" data-width=\"560\" data-height=\"315\">\r\n<div class=\"yt-video_container\">\r\n<h2 data-id=\"0-general-information\">General Information:</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>This license will be bound to your PC. No dongle or box is required.</li>\r\n<li>You can change a PC once per 48 hours (not more than 12 times during 6 months).</li>\r\n<li>The same license can be used on 2 PCs without switching limits.</li>\r\n<li>After the end of 6 month period you will have to buy this license again.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Note!</strong>&nbsp;Huawei phones released after March 2018 with new security (except models supported via test point) are&nbsp;<strong>NOT SUPPORTED</strong>.<br />Please follow future updates for more information.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"activate\" data-id=\"11-how-to-activate\">How to Activate:</h2>\r\n<p>To start using your digital license, please follow these steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Download the latest version of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://octoplusbox.com/en/download/software/\">Octoplus FRP Tool Installer</a></li>\r\n<li>Launch the software</li>\r\n<li>Use the received string to activate your digital license</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div class=\"full-img\"><img src=\"https://f00.psgsm.net/product/894333/screenshot-60.jpg\" alt=\"Software\" /></div>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"1-samsung-reset-frp-operations\">Samsung Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"2--reset-frp-uart-ufs-chips-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\">1. &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</h3>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation, do the following steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Put the phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold \"Volume-\" + \"Home\" + \"Power ON\" buttons) and connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Press &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; button.</li>\r\n<li>After Software request disconnect USB cable and connect Samsung Micro UART cable.</li>\r\n<li>Press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; keys for 15-20 seconds, Software will automatically close wizard window and will perform the reset FRP lock.</li>\r\n<li>Done.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"3--reset-frp-adb-combination-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\">2. &ldquo;Reset FRP ADB (Combination)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</h3>\r\n<p>To Reset FRP lock using combination firmware, you can try to do the following:</p>\r\n<p>I.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Write \"boot.img\" partition from appropriate Combination firmware.</li>\r\n<li>Perform \"Reset FRP ADB (Combination)\" operation in the software.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>II.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Write full Combination firmware.</li>\r\n<li>Go to \"Developer Options\" in the phone&rsquo;s Settings.</li>\r\n<li>Check \"Enable OEM ...\" option.</li>\r\n<li>Perform Factory Data Reset.</li>\r\n<li>Reflash the phone with full stock (original) firmware.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: \"boot.img\" from combination firmware can be not compatible with current phone\'s firmware. In that case phone will freeze on logo, or will be rebooting after writing of such boot. To restore the phone to its initial condition you need to reflash it with different full stock (original) firmware (or try to write only boot of such firmware).</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also note</strong>: You can write \"boot.img\" combination firmware or downgrade phone\'s firmware version only at your own risk!</p>\r\n<p>P.S. If you cannot find combination firmware for your model in &ldquo;SAMSUNG/COMBINATION\" folder in Support Area, this means we don&rsquo;t have these files at the moment. As soon as we get new combination firmwares, we will upload them into the Support Area.</p>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"4--reset-frp-download-mode-operation-be-careful-performing-this-operation-will-delete-all-user-data-contacts-pictures-and-other-from-the-device\">3. &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation will delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) from the device!</h3>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<p>1. Click \"Reset FRP (Download Mode)\" button.<br />2. Put phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Home&rdquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; buttons).<br />3. Connect the phone to PC via Micro USB cable.<br />4. Follow Software instructions (prompts).</p>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"5-huawei-reset-frp-operations\">Huawei Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation may reset/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.</li>\r\n<li>Put the phone in FastBoot Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; button, insert USB cable and wait until the phone goes in FastBoot Mode).</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"6-lg-reset-frp-operations\">LG Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be carefully, performing this operation may reset/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<p>1. Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<br />2. Put the phone in Download Mode (power the phone OFF, press and hold \"Vol+\" button and connect USB cable).<br />3. Install necessary driver.<br />4. Click \"Reset FRP\" button.<br />5. Follow software instructions (prompts).</p>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"7--alcatel-reset-frp-operations\">Alcatel Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Power the phone OFF and connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button.</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"8-motorola-reset-frp-operations\">Motorola Reset FRP operations.</h2>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</p>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Put the phone in Factory Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold \"Vol-\" + \"Power\" buttons; select &ldquo;Factory Mode&rdquo; in phone&rsquo;s menu and confirm selection; wait until the phone powers ON).</li>\r\n<li>Connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button.</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>Note: &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation may not work for some devices with latest Security patch level.</p>\r\n<p>* Developer provides support only for those phones which are on the list of supported. Not all servicing features can be applied to some supported models, due to difference of hardware / software versions.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>#shandy</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"widget_product_octopus-models\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[]', '{\"SERVICEID\":202,\"SERVICENAME\":\"Octoplus FRP 6 Month Digital License\",\"CREDIT\":\"47.0000\",\"INFO\":\"<p><strong>Octoplus FRP 6 Month Digital License<\\/strong>&nbsp;enables FRP reset operations for&nbsp;<strong>Samsung, Huawei, Xiaomi, LG, Alcatel, Motorola<\\/strong>&nbsp;cell phones.<\\/p>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"yt-video -inside-dom\\\" data-video-id=\\\"czL9Sp7hesA\\\" data-width=\\\"560\\\" data-height=\\\"315\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"yt-video_container\\\">\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"0-general-information\\\">General Information:<\\/h2>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li>This license will be bound to your PC. No dongle or box is required.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>You can change a PC once per 48 hours (not more than 12 times during 6 months).<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>The same license can be used on 2 PCs without switching limits.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>After the end of 6 month period you will have to buy this license again.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p><strong>Note!<\\/strong>&nbsp;Huawei phones released after March 2018 with new security (except models supported via test point) are&nbsp;<strong>NOT SUPPORTED<\\/strong>.<br \\/>Please follow future updates for more information.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 id=\\\"activate\\\" data-id=\\\"11-how-to-activate\\\">How to Activate:<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>To start using your digital license, please follow these steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Download the latest version of&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/octoplusbox.com\\/en\\/download\\/software\\/\\\">Octoplus FRP Tool Installer<\\/a><\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Launch the software<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Use the received string to activate your digital license<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"full-img\\\"><img src=\\\"https:\\/\\/f00.psgsm.net\\/product\\/894333\\/screenshot-60.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"Software\\\" \\/><\\/div>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"1-samsung-reset-frp-operations\\\">Samsung Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-id=\\\"2--reset-frp-uart-ufs-chips-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\\\">1. &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation, do the following steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Put the phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold \\\"Volume-\\\" + \\\"Home\\\" + \\\"Power ON\\\" buttons) and connect USB cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Press &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; button.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>After Software request disconnect USB cable and connect Samsung Micro UART cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; keys for 15-20 seconds, Software will automatically close wizard window and will perform the reset FRP lock.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Done.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h3 data-id=\\\"3--reset-frp-adb-combination-operation-this-operation-will-not-reset-delete-device-user-data\\\">2. &ldquo;Reset FRP ADB (Combination)&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p>To Reset FRP lock using combination firmware, you can try to do the following:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>I.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Write \\\"boot.img\\\" partition from appropriate Combination firmware.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Perform \\\"Reset FRP ADB (Combination)\\\" operation in the software.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p>II.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Write full Combination firmware.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Go to \\\"Developer Options\\\" in the phone&rsquo;s Settings.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Check \\\"Enable OEM ...\\\" option.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Perform Factory Data Reset.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Reflash the phone with full stock (original) firmware.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p><strong>Note<\\/strong>: \\\"boot.img\\\" from combination firmware can be not compatible with current phone\'s firmware. In that case phone will freeze on logo, or will be rebooting after writing of such boot. To restore the phone to its initial condition you need to reflash it with different full stock (original) firmware (or try to write only boot of such firmware).<\\/p>\\r\\n<p><strong>Also note<\\/strong>: You can write \\\"boot.img\\\" combination firmware or downgrade phone\'s firmware version only at your own risk!<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>P.S. If you cannot find combination firmware for your model in &ldquo;SAMSUNG\\/COMBINATION\\\" folder in Support Area, this means we don&rsquo;t have these files at the moment. As soon as we get new combination firmwares, we will upload them into the Support Area.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-id=\\\"4--reset-frp-download-mode-operation-be-careful-performing-this-operation-will-delete-all-user-data-contacts-pictures-and-other-from-the-device\\\">3. &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation will delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) from the device!<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP (Download Mode)&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>1. Click \\\"Reset FRP (Download Mode)\\\" button.<br \\/>2. Put phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Home&rdquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; buttons).<br \\/>3. Connect the phone to PC via Micro USB cable.<br \\/>4. Follow Software instructions (prompts).<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"5-huawei-reset-frp-operations\\\">Huawei Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation may reset\\/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Put the phone in FastBoot Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; button, insert USB cable and wait until the phone goes in FastBoot Mode).<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Install necessary driver.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"6-lg-reset-frp-operations\\\">LG Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be carefully, performing this operation may reset\\/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>1. Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<br \\/>2. Put the phone in Download Mode (power the phone OFF, press and hold \\\"Vol+\\\" button and connect USB cable).<br \\/>3. Install necessary driver.<br \\/>4. Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button.<br \\/>5. Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"7--alcatel-reset-frp-operations\\\">Alcatel Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Install necessary driver.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Power the phone OFF and connect USB cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h2 data-id=\\\"8-motorola-reset-frp-operations\\\">Motorola Reset FRP operations.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. This operation will not reset\\/delete device user data.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation, do the next steps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li>Put the phone in Factory Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold \\\"Vol-\\\" + \\\"Power\\\" buttons; select &ldquo;Factory Mode&rdquo; in phone&rsquo;s menu and confirm selection; wait until the phone powers ON).<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Connect USB cable.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Install necessary driver.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Click \\\"Reset FRP\\\" button.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p>Note: &ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation may not work for some devices with latest Security patch level.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>* Developer provides support only for those phones which are on the list of supported. Not all servicing features can be applied to some supported models, due to difference of hardware \\/ software versions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>#shandy<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"widget_product_octopus-models\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\",\"ADDITIONAL_NVP\":\"a:2:{s:13:\\\"hide_quantity\\\";i:0;s:13:\\\"quantity_rule\\\";a:4:{s:9:\\\"min_value\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:9:\\\"max_value\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:11:\\\"multiple_of\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:9:\\\"specified\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";}}\",\"TIME\":\"\",\"sync_key_data\":\"\",\"service_type_price_data\":\"\",\"qry_range_credit_info\":[{\"from_range\":1,\"to_range\":49,\"credit\":\"47.0000\"}],\"REQUIRED\":\"\"}', '{\"CUSTOM\":null}', '2026-02-25 03:00:52', '2026-02-25 03:00:52'),
(1185, 2, '113', 'Octoplus FRP Tool 1 Year Activation for a Box / Dongle', 'Gsm Server Products', 50.0000, NULL, '<h3>Octoplus FRP Tool 1 Year Activation for a Box / Dongle</h3>\r\n<p>Activation for&nbsp;<strong>Octopus Box, Octoplus Pro Box, Octoplus Box, Octoplus Dongle, Medusa Pro II Box, Medusa Pro Box</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Medusa Box</strong>&nbsp;enables FRP reset operations for&nbsp;<strong>Samsung, Huawei, Xiaomi, LG, Alcatel, Motorola</strong>&nbsp;cell phones.<br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\" /><br /></p>\r\n<p><strong>Access for 1 year.</strong></p>\r\n<h2 id=\"activate\" data-id=\"11-how-to-activate\"><a href=\"https://f00.psgsm.net/product/872882/manual-activate-frp-tool-new-eng.pdf\"><strong>How to Activate Octoplus FRP Tool?</strong></a></h2>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"0-reset-frp-for-samsung\">Reset FRP for Samsung</h2>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"1--reset-frp-uart-ufs-chips\">1. Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)</h3>\r\n<div class=\"notification info\">\r\n<p><strong>This operation WILL NOT reset/delete device user data</strong>.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>To perform &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; operation, do the following steps:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Put the phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold \"Volume-\" + \"Home\" + \"Power ON\" buttons) and connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Press &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (UFS chips)&rdquo; button.</li>\r\n<li>After Software request disconnect USB cable and connect Samsung Micro UART cable.</li>\r\n<li>Press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; keys for 15-20 seconds, Software will automatically close wizard window and will perform the reset FRP lock.</li>\r\n<li>Done.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"2--reset-frp-adb-combination\">2. Reset FRP ADB (Combination)</h3>\r\n<div class=\"notification info\">\r\n<p><strong>This operation WILL NOT reset/delete device user data.</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>To Reset FRP lock using combination firmware, you can try to do the following:</p>\r\n<p>I.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Write \"boot.img\" partition from appropriate Combination firmware.</li>\r\n<li>Perform \"Reset FRP ADB (Combination)\" operation in the software.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>II.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Write full Combination firmware.</li>\r\n<li>Go to \"Developer Options\" in the phone&rsquo;s Settings.</li>\r\n<li>Check \"Enable OEM ...\" option.</li>\r\n<li>Perform Factory Data Reset.</li>\r\n<li>Reflash the phone with full stock (original) firmware.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: \"boot.img\" from combination firmware can be not compatible with current phone\'s firmware. In that case phone will freeze on logo, or will be rebooting after writing of such boot. To restore the phone to its initial condition you need to reflash it with different full stock (original) firmware (or try to write only boot of such firmware).</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also note</strong>: You can write \"boot.img\" combination firmware or downgrade phone\'s firmware version only at your own risk!</p>\r\n<p>P.S. If you cannot find combination firmware for your model in &ldquo;SAMSUNG/COMBINATION\" folder in Support Area, this means we don&rsquo;t have these files at the moment. As soon as we get new combination firmwares, we will upload them into the Support Area.</p>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"3--reset-frp-download-mode\">3. Reset FRP (Download Mode)</h3>\r\n<div class=\"notification warning\">\r\n<p><strong>Be careful, performing this operation WILL DELETE all user data (contacts, pictures and other) from the device!</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>To perform the Reset FRP (Download Mode) operation, do the following:</p>\r\n<p>1. Click \"Reset FRP (Download Mode)\" button.<br />2. Put phone in Download Mode (power off the phone, press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; + &ldquo;Home&rdquo; + &ldquo;Power ON&rdquo; buttons).<br />3. Connect the phone to PC via Micro USB cable.<br />4. Follow Software instructions (prompts).</p>\r\n<h3 data-id=\"4--reset-frp-uart-emmc-chips\">4. Reset FRP UART (eMMC chips)</h3>\r\n<div class=\"notification info\">\r\n<p><strong>This operation WILL NOT reset/delete user data on the device.</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>To perform the Reset FRP UART (eMMC chips) operation, do the following:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Click &ldquo;Reset FRP UART (eMMC chips)&rdquo; button</li>\r\n<li>Connect the phone to Box via UART cable</li>\r\n<li>Press and hold \"Vol-\" and \"Power\" buttons for 15-20 seconds</li>\r\n<li>Wait until software requests to connect USB cable</li>\r\n<li>Connect the phone to PC via USB cable. Software will read some data</li>\r\n<li>Connect again the phone to Box via UART cable</li>\r\n<li>Press and hold \"Vol-\" and \"Power\" buttons for 15-20 seconds</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts)</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"5-reset-frp-for-huawei\">Reset FRP for Huawei</h2>\r\n<div class=\"notification warning\">\r\n<p>Be careful, performing this operation may reset/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>To perform the Reset FRP operation, do the following:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.</li>\r\n<li>Put the phone in FastBoot Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold &ldquo;Volume-&ldquo; button, insert USB cable and wait until the phone goes in FastBoot Mode).</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"6-reset-frp-for-lg\">Reset FRP for LG</h2>\r\n<div class=\"notification warning\">\r\n<p>&ldquo;Reset FRP&rdquo; operation. Be careful, performing this operation may reset/delete all user data (contacts, pictures and other) on some devices and firmware versions! Software will inform you about this in log, so please read and follow software instructions (prompts) carefully!</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>To perform the Reset FRP operation, do the following:</p>\r\n<p>1. Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.<br />2. Put the phone in Download Mode (power the phone OFF, press and hold \"Vol+\" button and connect USB cable).<br />3. Install necessary driver.<br />4. Click \"Reset FRP\" button.<br />5. Follow software instructions (prompts).</p>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"7-reset-frp-for-alcatel\"><strong>Reset FRP for Alcatel</strong></h2>\r\n<div class=\"notification info\">\r\n<p>This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>To perform the Reset FRP operation, do the following:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Remove SD and SIM cards from the phone.</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Power the phone OFF and connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button.</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"8-reset-frp-for-motorola\">Reset FRP for Motorola</h2>\r\n<div class=\"notification info\">\r\n<p>This operation will not reset/delete device user data.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>To perform the Reset FRP operation, do the following:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Put the phone in Factory Mode (power the phone OFF; press and hold \"Vol-\" + \"Power\" buttons; select &ldquo;Factory Mode&rdquo; in phone&rsquo;s menu and confirm selection; wait until the phone powers ON).</li>\r\n<li>Connect USB cable.</li>\r\n<li>Install necessary driver.</li>\r\n<li>Click \"Reset FRP\" button.</li>\r\n<li>Follow software instructions (prompts).</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div class=\"notification\">\r\n<p>Reset FRP operation may not work for some devices with the latest Security patch level.</p>\r\n<h2 data-id=\"11-package-contents\">Package Contents</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Activation Code for Octoplus FRP Tool</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>The product is digital - no packaging!</strong></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>#shandy</strong></p>\r\n</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[]', '{\"SERVICEID\":113,\"SERVICENAME\":\"Octoplus FRP Tool 1 Year Activation 