(1537, 2, '832', 'Fast Cron Job [ Active License 30 - 90 - 365 Days ]', 'CronJob', 8.5000, '1-5 Minutes', '<h2>Note :</h2>\r\n<h2>1 QNT&nbsp; To =&nbsp;<strong>Basic Package</strong>&nbsp;Domain Unlimited...✅<br />3 QNT&nbsp; To =&nbsp;<strong>Silver Package</strong>&nbsp;Domain Unlimited...✅<br />5 QNT&nbsp; To =&nbsp;<strong>Premium Package</strong>&nbsp;Domain Unlimited...✅<br /><br />Save your time by working&nbsp;<span class=\"home__theme\">with</span>&nbsp;FastCronJob</h2>\r\n<p>FastCronJob makes it easy to create and manage cronjobs for multiple websites, with your team.<br />Know when your cron jobs are executed, get failure notifications.</p>\r\n<h2>No need to add Cron Jobs AnyWhere Just Add Your Domain &amp; It Start Works<br /><strong><br />Register Your Account</strong>&nbsp;:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.fastcronjob.com/\">https://www.fastcronjob.com</a><br /><br />If you are a Dhru Fusion website owner, it sounds like you need a cron job service that runs at various intervals (5 seconds, 10 seconds, 15 seconds, 25 seconds). First, you\'ll need to set up your services on fastcronjob.com to handle the specified intervals. Assuming you can configure the cron jobs on this server, you can set up endpoints for your GET and POST requests.<br /><br />To set endpoints, there is no need to manually add any URL. Just add your domain name sign-up time, and all services will automatically become active in 10 seconds, 15 seconds, 25 seconds for GET and POST requests.<br /><br />You can also add URL endpoints for Dhru Fusion price updates. This will automatically update the prices on your website at intervals like 30 minutes or 60 minutes. However, the price update URL endpoints need to be added manually.<br />Check Server Logs: Verify that your server logs show the tasks being executed at the correct intervals.<br /><br />If a task does not run, check the cron job configuration on fastcronjob.com and ensure the endpoint URLs are correct.<br />This setup will help you achieve the desired cron job functionality with fast execution intervals. If you encounter any issues, refer to the documentation of fastcronjob.com or your server setup for additional troubleshooting steps.</h2>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>#shandy</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, '[]', '{\"SERVICEID\":832,\"SERVICENAME\":\"Fast Cron Job [ Active License 30 - 90 - 365 Days ]\",\"CREDIT\":\"8.5000\",\"INFO\":\"<h2>Note :<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h2>1 QNT&nbsp; To =&nbsp;<strong>Basic Package<\\/strong>&nbsp;Domain Unlimited...\\u2705<br \\/>3 QNT&nbsp; To =&nbsp;<strong>Silver Package<\\/strong>&nbsp;Domain Unlimited...\\u2705<br \\/>5 QNT&nbsp; To =&nbsp;<strong>Premium Package<\\/strong>&nbsp;Domain Unlimited...\\u2705<br \\/><br \\/>Save your time by working&nbsp;<span class=\\\"home__theme\\\">with<\\/span>&nbsp;FastCronJob<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>FastCronJob makes it easy to create and manage cronjobs for multiple websites, with your team.<br \\/>Know when your cron jobs are executed, get failure notifications.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2>No need to add Cron Jobs AnyWhere Just Add Your Domain &amp; It Start Works<br \\/><strong><br \\/>Register Your Account<\\/strong>&nbsp;:&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.fastcronjob.com\\/\\\">https:\\/\\/www.fastcronjob.com<\\/a><br \\/><br \\/>If you are a Dhru Fusion website owner, it sounds like you need a cron job service that runs at various intervals (5 seconds, 10 seconds, 15 seconds, 25 seconds). First, you\'ll need to set up your services on fastcronjob.com to handle the specified intervals. Assuming you can configure the cron jobs on this server, you can set up endpoints for your GET and POST requests.<br \\/><br \\/>To set endpoints, there is no need to manually add any URL. Just add your domain name sign-up time, and all services will automatically become active in 10 seconds, 15 seconds, 25 seconds for GET and POST requests.<br \\/><br \\/>You can also add URL endpoints for Dhru Fusion price updates. This will automatically update the prices on your website at intervals like 30 minutes or 60 minutes. However, the price update URL endpoints need to be added manually.<br \\/>Check Server Logs: Verify that your server logs show the tasks being executed at the correct intervals.<br \\/><br \\/>If a task does not run, check the cron job configuration on fastcronjob.com and ensure the endpoint URLs are correct.<br \\/>This setup will help you achieve the desired cron job functionality with fast execution intervals. If you encounter any issues, refer to the documentation of fastcronjob.com or your server setup for additional troubleshooting steps.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>#shandy<\\/p>\",\"ADDITIONAL_NVP\":\"a:2:{s:13:\\\"hide_quantity\\\";i:0;s:13:\\\"quantity_rule\\\";a:4:{s:9:\\\"min_value\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:9:\\\"max_value\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:11:\\\"multiple_of\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";s:9:\\\"specified\\\";s:0:\\\"\\\";}}\",\"TIME\":\"1-5 Minutes\",\"sync_key_data\":\"\",\"service_type_price_data\":\"\",\"qry_range_credit_info\":[{\"from_range\":1,\"to_range\":10000,\"credit\":\"8.5000\"}],\"REQUIRED\":\"Enter Your Email Address\"}', '{\"CUSTOM\":null}', '2026-02-25 03:00:52', '2026-02-25 03:00:52'),
